<script setup>
/**
 * Angelus Novus, traced from Klee's plate and drawn in the site's ink.
 *
 * Paul Klee, 1920, monoprint. Klee died in 1940, so the work is public domain
 * in the EU and the UK, and in the US as a work published before 1929. The
 * plate this came from is the Israel Museum's, via Wikimedia Commons.
 *
 * Not a picture of the painting: the contours of Klee's ink were traced from a
 * 1920px reproduction, everything that ran to the edge of the plate thrown away
 * — the corner blooms, the scuffed ground, the signature, none of which is the
 * figure — and what was left simplified and corner-cut until it read as a mark
 * rather than as a scan. It carries no colour of its own. The ink is
 * `currentColor` and the ring punched around each pupil is `var(--a-bg)`, so
 * the whole thing turns over with the theme like everything else here.
 *
 * The eyes are the reason for the rings. At this weight the ink either side of
 * a pupil closes over it, and Benjamin's angel is defined by what it is looking
 * at — an angel that is not staring is the wrong drawing.
 */
</script>

